---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import LearnLayout from '../../layouts/LearnLayout.astro';
import { tutorials } from '../../data/tutorials';
import hero from '../../assets/screens/harbor-blender-previs.jpg';
---

<LearnLayout title="Renku Tutorials — From screenplay to screen" description="A practical filmmaking course: Inspiration, Lookbooks, Cast, Locations, Props, Scene Beats, Storyboards, Shot Lists, Blender Previs, and AI video generation." current="tutorials">
  <header class="container learn-hero learn-split">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The first-scene guide</p><h1>From a spark<br />to the <em>screen.</em></h1><p class="lede">Make one scene, all the way through. Find its visual language, build its world, and direct a take worth keeping.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/tutorials/inspiration/">Start with inspiration</a><a class="text-link" href="#chapters">Browse chapters</a></div><div class="learn-meta"><span>8 focused chapters + an optional guide</span><span>Your screenplay · Your pace</span></div></div>
    <figure class="learn-image"><Image src={hero} alt="A harbor scene moving from Blender staging to a cinematic generated take." widths={[800, 1200, 1600]} sizes="50vw" loading="eager" /><figcaption>A scene, from the first camera decision to its cinematic interpretation.</figcaption></figure>
  </header>
  <section class="container" id="chapters" style="scroll-margin-top: 6rem">
    <div class="lesson-section"><h2>Give direction. The skills handle the workflow.</h2><p>Start with what you want to make or change. The Movie Director skill coordinates work across departments, and Codex can also route a focused request from the specialist skills’ descriptions. Each chapter names the skills involved so you know what they do; you do not need to include their names in your prompts.</p><p>The examples are starting points. Add your own references, questions, or creative constraints, then review the result in Studio and ask for another pass. Creating Inspiration folders and adding images happens directly in Studio.</p></div>
    <div class="course-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The creative path</p><h2>Build the film in layers.</h2></div><p>New to Renku? <a class="text-link" href="/quick-start/">Complete Quick Start first.</a></p></div>
    <div class="chapter-grid">{tutorials.filter((tutorial) => !tutorial.optional).map((tutorial, index) => <a class="chapter-card" href={`/tutorials/${tutorial.slug}/`}><Image src={tutorial.image} alt={tutorial.alt} widths={[480, 720, 1000]} sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 33vw, 50vw" /><div class="chapter-card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">0{index + 1} · {tutorial.phase}</span><h3>{tutorial.title}</h3><p>{tutorial.description}</p><span class="chapter-link">Read chapter {index + 1}</span></div></a>)}</div>
    <div class="next-lesson"><div><p class="eyebrow">Two ways to plan</p><h2>Compose the coverage. Or stage the motion.</h2><p>Follow chapters 1–5, then choose Shot List or Blender Previs. Both lead to video generation.</p></div><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/tutorials/shot-list/">Explore shot planning</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="container" id="optional">
    <div class="course-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Optional · When you need it</p><h2>Expand your model choices.</h2></div><p>Come back here when a model you want is missing. You can complete the filmmaking guide without this step.</p></div>
    <div class="chapter-grid">{tutorials.filter((tutorial) => tutorial.optional).map((tutorial) => <a class="chapter-card" href={`/tutorials/${tutorial.slug}/`}><Image src={tutorial.image} alt={tutorial.alt} widths={[480, 720, 1000]} sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 33vw, 50vw" /><div class="chapter-card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Optional guide</span><h3>{tutorial.title}</h3><p>{tutorial.description}</p><span class="chapter-link">Read optional guide</span></div></a>)}</div>
  </section>
</LearnLayout>
